;;
;; REPL/RedTeam/[RT-I]_GasStation.repl — FAMILY I: the gas station's payable surface.
;;
;; "What will Ouronet agree to pay for?"
;;
;; This is the last first-rank target Stage 0 produced and the only one never attacked. Stage 0's
;; own words: "`GAS_PAYER` Case 3 validates exec-code forms 0, 1 and 2 only; forms at index >= 3
;; are unconstrained and form 2 need only *start with* `(let`. The only bound is economic."
;;
;; GAS_PAYER is the capability the gas station acquires before agreeing to pay a transaction's KDA.
;; Its whole input is `(read-msg "exec-code")`, so `env-data` IS the fixture and `test-capability`
;; acquires the cap exactly as chainweb would during buy-gas. The idiom is borrowed from
;; modules/DALOS-ADMIN.repl <<DALOS-G2a>>.
;;
;; Run: cd REPL && pact "RedTeam/[RT-I]_GasStation.repl"
;;
(load "../deploy-stage00.repl")
(load "../deploy-stage01.repl")

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-I-001a - BASELINE: the intended Case 3 shape is funded")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [RT-I-001a] ---")
;;<<RT-I-001>> FAMILY: I | STATUS: SUCCEEDED
;;HYPOTHESIS: the Ouronet gas station whitelists by reading the transaction's top-level forms out of
;;            `exec-code`. Case 1 pins a SINGLE form to `(coin.C_`, `(ouronet-ns.TS`,
;;            `(ouronet-ns.DSP` or `(ouronet-ns.STOAICO.`; Case 2 pins BOTH of two forms to
;;            `(coin.C_`. Case 3 accepts `(>= n 3)` and then inspects indices 0, 1 and 2 ONLY. If an
;;            attacker supplies the three-form prefix Case 3 wants and APPENDS a fourth form, that
;;            form is never looked at -- and Ouronet pays the gas for whatever it is. The appended
;;            code still has to satisfy its own guards, so this is not theft; it is FREE EXECUTION,
;;            which is the thing a gas station exists to ration.
;;METHOD:     drive `DALOS.GAS_PAYER` directly with `env-data` supplying `exec-code`, exactly as
;;            chainweb supplies it during buy-gas -- the idiom modules/DALOS-ADMIN.repl
;;            <<DALOS-G2a>> establishes. ONE TRANSACTION PER CASE, because `test-capability` grants
;;            the cap for the remainder of the transaction. Then PRICE the door by measuring a real
;;            `IGNIS::C_Collect` of `UDC_CustomCodeCumulator`, for a standard patron and for a
;;            gassless one.
;;
;;RESULT: SUCCEEDED, and the defect is NOT the unvalidated tail -- that is the custom-code door
;;        working as designed, with the fee as its bound. The defect is that THE FEE CAN BE
;;        DECLINED. Every link measured below:
;;
;;  1. Case 3 inspects forms 0, 1, 2 only; `(>= n 3)` bounds nothing above.   [RT-I-001c]
;;  2. The COUNT of appended forms is unbounded.                              [RT-I-001d]
;;  3. Form 2 need only START with "(let" -- its body is unread.              [RT-I-001e]
;;  4. The door is priced at a FLAT (* 5.0 tier-biggest): 25 raw, 13.25 after
;;     a top-tier discount -- independent of what the tail does.              [RT-I-001f]
;;  5. A GASSLESS (smart) account pays 0.0. `IGNIS::C_Collect` collects only
;;     `(if (and (!= ignis-sum 0.0) (not iz-gassles-patron)) ...)`.           [RT-I-001g]
;;  6. Smart accounts are PERMISSIONLESS: `DALOS|C_DeploySmartAccount` is a CLIENT wrapper on
;;     TS01-C1:311, not an admin one, priced in STOA at `acct-smart` 1000 deter = 100 STOA (~$10)
;;     -- and that fee is itself conditional on `UR_AccountCreationStoa`, so it is ZERO when the
;;     account-creation toggle is off.
;;
;;  So: pay once (or nothing), then submit unlimited transactions of the shape
;;  `namespace + IGNIS.C_Collect(CustomCodeCumulator) + (let ...) + <arbitrary code>`, paying NO
;;  IGNIS, with Ouronet funding up to DALOS|GAS-BUDGET = 2,000,000 gas units of KDA each time.
;;
;;  THIS IS RT-A-001's SHAPE IN THE GAS STATION: a deterrent that can be declined. There the second
;;  door skipped `lp-churn`; here the gassless exemption skips the custom-code fee. The appended
;;  code still satisfies its own guards, so it is not theft -- it is FREE EXECUTION, which is the
;;  one thing a gas station exists to ration.
;;
;;SCOPE OF WHAT IS PROVEN. Links 1-5 are measured in this file; link 6 is read off the Talos surface.
;;The COMPOSITION is not executed end to end, because the REPL cannot simulate chainweb's buy-gas
;;phase -- `test-capability` acquires GAS_PAYER exactly as buy-gas would, which is what makes 1-3
;;real, but no REPL can show the KDA actually leaving the station. That last step is an on-chain
;;smoke test, and it is the only part of this finding that is inference rather than measurement.
;;
;;ONE TRANSACTION PER CASE, AND THAT IS NOT COSMETIC. The first draft of this attack put all five
;;cases in ONE begin-tx and reported a clean success. It was vacuous: `test-capability` GRANTS the
;;capability for the remainder of the transaction, so cases 2-5 never re-evaluated the defcap body
;;at all -- they were reading a cap already in scope from case 1. The CONTROL is what exposed it:
;;a single foreign form, which DALOS-G2c proves is refused, came back as "expected failure, got
;;result: ()". Without that control this file would have claimed a gas-station hole it had not
;;demonstrated. Capability scope is per-transaction; so is each case below.
;;BASELINE. Without this the refusals below prove nothing -- a Case 3 that rejects everything is not
;;a hole, it is a closed door.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(env-data { "exec-code": ["(namespace \"ouronet-ns\")"
                   "(IGNIS.C_Collect \"Ѻ.attacker\" (IGNIS.UDC_CustomCodeCumulator))"
                   "(let ((x 1)) x)"] })
(print
    (expect "<<RT-I-001>> BASELINE: the intended three-form Case 3 shape is funded"
        true (!= "" (format "{}" [(test-capability (DALOS.GAS_PAYER KST.EMMA 1000 0.0000001))])))
)
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(env-data {})
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-I-001b - CONTROL: a single foreign form is refused")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [RT-I-001b] ---")
;;CONTROL. Case 1 really is tight, so the station is not simply open to everything; the only
;;question is what Case 3 lets past. This is the assertion that caught the vacuous first draft.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(env-data { "exec-code": ["(bogus.thing)"] })
(print
    (expect-failure "<<RT-I-001>> CONTROL: a single foreign form is refused by Case 1"
        "Payable Modules / form count not satisfied"
        (test-capability (DALOS.GAS_PAYER KST.EMMA 1000 0.0000001)))
)
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(env-data {})
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-I-001c - ATTACK: a fourth, unvalidated form")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [RT-I-001c] ---")
;;THE ATTACK. Identical prefix, one extra form at index 3 that no enforce in Case 3 ever reads.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(env-data { "exec-code": ["(namespace \"ouronet-ns\")"
                   "(IGNIS.C_Collect \"Ѻ.attacker\" (IGNIS.UDC_CustomCodeCumulator))"
                   "(let ((x 1)) x)"
                   "(bogus.thing)"] })
(print
    (expect "<<RT-I-001>> ATTACK: a FOURTH form of arbitrary code rides in unvalidated"
        true (!= "" (format "{}" [(test-capability (DALOS.GAS_PAYER KST.EMMA 1000 0.0000001))])))
)
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(env-data {})
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-I-001d - ATTACK: the appended count is unbounded")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [RT-I-001d] ---")
;;...and it is not a one-form allowance. `(>= n 3)` bounds nothing above.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(env-data { "exec-code": ["(namespace \"ouronet-ns\")"
                   "(IGNIS.C_Collect \"Ѻ.attacker\" (IGNIS.UDC_CustomCodeCumulator))"
                   "(let ((x 1)) x)"
                   "(bogus.one)" "(bogus.two)" "(bogus.three)"] })
(print
    (expect "<<RT-I-001>> ATTACK: neither is the COUNT of appended forms bounded"
        true (!= "" (format "{}" [(test-capability (DALOS.GAS_PAYER KST.EMMA 1000 0.0000001))])))
)
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(env-data {})
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-I-001e - ATTACK: form 2's body is unread")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [RT-I-001e] ---")
;;A SECOND, INDEPENDENT way past the same case: the form-2 check is `(take 4 ...)` = "(let", so
;;everything after those four characters is free.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(env-data { "exec-code": ["(namespace \"ouronet-ns\")"
                   "(IGNIS.C_Collect \"Ѻ.attacker\" (IGNIS.UDC_CustomCodeCumulator))"
                   "(let ((y 0)) (bogus.thing))"] })
(print
    (expect "<<RT-I-001>> ATTACK: form 2 need only START with (let -- its body is unread"
        true (!= "" (format "{}" [(test-capability (DALOS.GAS_PAYER KST.EMMA 1000 0.0000001))])))
)
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(env-data {})
(commit-tx)
;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-I-001f - what the unvalidated tail actually COSTS the attacker")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [RT-I-001f · the price of the custom-code door] ---")
;;THE ECONOMICS, WHICH DECIDE WHETHER THE HOLE MATTERS. Case 3 is not an oversight in shape: it is
;;the CUSTOM CODE door, and it obliges the caller to run
;;`(IGNIS.C_Collect "Ѻ.…" (IGNIS.UDC_CustomCodeCumulator))` as form 1. That cumulator is
;;`(* 5.0 (UC_IgnisLeg "tier-biggest"))` -- a FLAT fee, independent of how much work the appended
;;forms do, while the gas Ouronet subsidises is bounded only by DALOS|GAS-BUDGET (2,000,000 units at
;;the protocol floor, per UEV_enforce-notional-at-floor).
;;
;;So the question is not "can arbitrary code ride in" -- RT-I-001c proves it can -- but "what is the
;;exchange rate". Measured here rather than asserted, because a flat fee against a bounded subsidy
;;is only a defect if the fee is the smaller number.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-IGNIS:module{IgnisCollectorV2} IGNIS)
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
    )
    (let
        (
            (b0:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
        )
        (ref-IGNIS::C_Collect patron (ref-IGNIS::UDC_CustomCodeCumulator))
        (let
            (
                (paid:decimal (- b0 (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false)))
            )
            (map print
                [
                    (format "<<RT-I-001>> custom-code door costs the caller {} IGNIS, and unlocks up to {} gas"
                        [paid DALOS.DALOS|GAS-BUDGET])
                    ;;the door is PRICED -- a free door would make the unvalidated tail serious
                    (expect "<<RT-I-001>> the custom-code door is not free: the caller really is charged"
                        true (> paid 0.0))
                    ;;...and the fee is FLAT. This is the property that makes the exchange rate
                    ;;attacker-controlled: identical fee whether the tail does nothing or 2M gas of work.
                    (expect "<<RT-I-001>> the fee is the FLAT 5x tier-biggest, not a function of the work"
                        (* (ref-DALOS::URC_IgnisGasDiscount patron) (* 5.0 (ref-IGNIS::UC_IgnisLeg "tier-biggest")))
                        paid)
                ])
        )
    )
    ""
)
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)
;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-I-001g - does a GASSLESS patron pay for the custom-code door at all?")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [RT-I-001g · the exemption underneath the fee] ---")
;;THE FEE HAS AN EXEMPTION, AND IT IS THE WHOLE QUESTION. `IGNIS::C_Collect` collects only when
;;    (if (and (!= ignis-sum 0.0) (not iz-gassles-patron)) ...)
;;where `iz-gassles-patron` is `(DALOS::UR_AccountType patron)` -- the SMART-ACCOUNT flag. If a smart
;;account pays nothing, then RT-I-001f's 13.25 IGNIS is not the price of the custom-code door; it is
;;the price for STANDARD accounts only, and the door is FREE for anyone who deploys a smart account.
;;
;;The discount cannot get there on its own: UC_GasDiscount is (7*(major-1) + minor) percent, so at
;;the top tier seen in this harness (major 7) the cost floor is ~51%, never zero. The exemption is a
;;different mechanism and it is binary.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }, { "key": "PK_BJ", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-IGNIS:module{IgnisCollectorV2} IGNIS)
        (smart:string KC.BJ)
    )
    (let
        (
            (iz-smart:bool (ref-DALOS::UR_AccountType smart))
            (b0:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply smart false))
        )
        (ref-IGNIS::C_Collect smart (ref-IGNIS::UDC_CustomCodeCumulator))
        (let
            (
                (paid:decimal (- b0 (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply smart false)))
            )
            (map print
                [
                    (format "<<RT-I-001>> smart-account patron: iz-gassless={} paid={} IGNIS" [iz-smart paid])
                    ;;non-vacuity: the account really is the gassless kind, so a zero below means the
                    ;;exemption fired and not that the fixture picked an ordinary account.
                    (expect "<<RT-I-001>> the fixture really is a gassless (smart) account"
                        true iz-smart)
                    ;;THE FINDING, whichever way it lands -- stated as a measurement, not a guess.
                    (expect "<<RT-I-001>> ...and this is what the custom-code door costs it"
                        0.0 paid)
                ])
        )
    )
    ""
)
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)
